{"url" : "https://x.com/willcb/status/2089774397007810702", "canonical_url" : "https://x.com/willcb/status/2089774397007810702", "title" : "will brown (@willcb)", "clean_title" : "", "summary" : "always super exciting to see the open RL ecosystem thrive 🚀\nmiles v0.1 ships with first-class support for training with `verifiers` envs :)\n@primeintellect 🤝 @radixark\nQuoting @radixark\nToday we're launching Miles v0.1, an open-source RL framework for LLMs and multimodal models.\nRL training is easy to start and hard to debug. Miles helps you ensure your run is correct, use hardware efficiently, and keep RL running at scale.\nOver the past 9 months, 72 contributors have landed 1,326 commits, 85 GPU E2E CI tests, battle-testing Miles on frontier open models like Kimi K3, DeepSeek V4, Qwen 3.8, GLM 5.2, Inkling, MiniMax H3, etc.\nMiles powers frontier-model development and production RL workloads at @humansand, @periodiclabs, @modal, @DecagonAI, @Eigent_AI, @nebiusai, @IBM and more, on both @NVIDIAAI and @AIatAMD hardware.\nHere is what we built, and why teams picked Miles🧵\n🎬 https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2089742959394914304/img/dZir408p86wB1Nwi.jpg | https://video-s.twimg.com/amplify_video/2089742959394914304/vid/avc1/480x270/AmS_sdGjAVIobjd_.mp4?tag=29", "clean_summary" : "", "date" : "2026-08-18", "tags" : ["twitter"], "extra_tags" : [], "source" : "twitter", "source_url" : null, "urls" : [], "linked_urls" : [], "link_hosts" : [], "citation_count" : null, "twitter_likes" : 129, "twitter_retweets" : 6, "twitter_replies" : 9, "twitter_quotes" : 0, "twitter_views" : 12612, "twitter_bookmarks" : 36, "referenced_author" : "radixark", "created_at" : "2026-10-07T19:13:20Z"}
