{"url" : "https://x.com/willcb/status/2090135226030956653", "canonical_url" : "https://x.com/willcb/status/2090135226030956653", "title" : "will brown (@willcb)", "clean_title" : "", "summary" : "tap in we’re scaling self-verification\nQuoting @hwchase17\ntop tier webinar tmrw!\n@Vtrivedy10 (@LangChain) @willcb (@PrimeIntellect) @AEllisBloor (@baseten) and I will will be jamming on how to automate more parts of the agent improvement loop (eval and environment engineering in particular)\nCome join us:\n📷 https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HQGmLJAaAAAs1Ch.jpg", "clean_summary" : "", "date" : "2026-08-19", "tags" : ["twitter"], "extra_tags" : [], "source" : "twitter", "source_url" : null, "urls" : [], "linked_urls" : [{"url": "https://events.langchain.com/webinar/Towards-Automating-Eval-and-Environment-Engineering/", "host": "events.langchain.com", "image": "https://staticassets.public-pr50.goldcast.io/public_images/events/ddb2f1f1-ba33-4f16-8808-f3afbf6ac7e4/LQ8mC2NkT1VgLPzmXnKg_Towards_Automating_Eval_and_Environment_Engineering.png", "title": "", "summary": "Evals are training data for agents. Teams can fit agent behavior to them through harness engineering such as changing prompts & tools or fine-tuning. The eval provides a fixed target for deciding whether those changes improved the intended capability.LangChain recently launched the Eval Engineering Skill, which helps coding agents use repository context and agent traces to propose and build executable evals in Harbor format.Part of this is giving builders the tools to model agent behavior in realistic environments.Join us for a live panel discussion on how coding agents can automate more of the eval engineering workflow while keeping developers involved in the design and review process.Topics will include:What parts of eval engineering can be automated?How can production traces become repeatable evals?Why is human feedback still critical to eval design?How can teams detect reward hacking and weak verifiers?Why do reproducible, containerized environments matter?"}], "link_hosts" : ["events.langchain.com"], "citation_count" : null, "twitter_likes" : 89, "twitter_retweets" : 10, "twitter_replies" : 2, "twitter_quotes" : 1, "twitter_views" : 13588, "twitter_bookmarks" : 28, "referenced_author" : "hwchase17", "created_at" : "2026-10-07T19:42:15Z"}
